                <pb facs="1543" n="1527" sameAs="frus:frus1949v06/pg1527"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>The <hi rendition="#italic">Ad Hoc</hi> Political Committee made its report to
                    the General Assembly on December 7; for its text, see United Nations, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Official Records of the Fourth Session of the General
                        Assembly, Plenary Meetings of the General Assembly, Annex to the Summary
                        Records of Meetings, 1949</hi> (hereinafter identified as GA, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">4th sess., Plenary, Annex</hi>), page 35. The report
                    included two draft resolutions adopted by the Committee for consideration by the
                    General Assembly. One concerned the questions of an international regime for the
                    Jerusalem area and of the protection of the Holy Places, the Committee adopting
                    the recommendations of Subcommittee 1 by a vote of 35 to 13, with 11
                    abstentions. <pb facs="1544" n="1528" xml:id="pg1528"/> The second draft
                    resolution dealt with the question of assistance to the Palestine refugees,
                    which the Committee adopted by 48 votes to none, with 6 abstentions. For the
                    texts of the two draft resolutions, see GA, <hi rendition="#italic">4th Sess.,
                        Plenary, Annex</hi>, pages 38 and 39. For the proceedings of the Committee
                    from December 5 to 7, see GA, <hi rendition="#italic">4th sess., Ad Hoc
                        Political Committee</hi>, pages 339–368.</p>
            </div>
